    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sxuedu/jobs/5202584/dean-of-the-school-of-nursing-and-health-sciences": {
      "title": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences Salary $145,000.00 - $160,000.00 Annually Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number 01406 Department Academic Affairs Opening Date 05/28/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Dean provides operational and academic leadership, overseeing all programs, faculty, budgets, and strategic vision for the School of Nursing and Health Sciences (SONHS), ensuring quality education, regulatory and accreditation compliance, student success, and community partnerships to meet current and evolving healthcare needs. By pursuing opportunities and anticipating opportunities yet to come, the Dean helps advance the SONHS and the broader University. Essential Duties & Responsibilities • Implement the University’s mission as a Catholic Institution founded by the Sisters of Mercy. • Advance governing Board-approved strategic priorities and participate in strategic planning implementation teams, including exploration of efficient and effective academic structures within SONHS. • Prioritize academic programs to better serve students and enhance academic standing and financial sustainability. • Collaborate with Enrollment, Advancement, and Alumni Services to support the continued success and growth of nursing programs. • Build and maintain partnerships with community and nursing leaders to advance program growth, ensure access to clinical placements, and create employment pathways for graduates. • Institutionalize strong academic policies and processes related to program review, curricular effectiveness and efficiency, assessment of student learning outcomes, and internal reallocation of resources. • Assess University operations for efficiency and effectiveness in serving students. • Hire, develop, and retain highly capable faculty and staff who are results-driven in mission integration, program development, recruitment, retention, advising, mentoring, completion, and alumni success. • Implement effective faculty and staff development and evaluation processes, including substantive post-tenure review. • Oversee academic programs and ensure the maintenance of institutional and specialized accreditation. • Serve as Chief Nurse Officer in relation to regulatory and accreditation standards and requirements. • Exercise leadership within SONHS, the Faculty Senate, and University committees in collaboration with faculty colleagues. • Implement University policies, procedures, directives, and Service Excellence Philosophy and Standards. • Develop effective partnerships and communication with the Provost and President to accomplish strategic priorities. • Model and uphold the highest professional standards, fostering a respectful, diverse work and learning environment consistent with the University’s Core Values. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Provost and President. This position offers a moving allowance of up to $2,000 to defray moving expenses. Qualifications • Graduate degree in nursing and a terminal degree in nursing or a related field from an accredited institution of higher learning. • Registered Nurse or eligible for licensure in the State of Illinois. • Minimum of five (5) years of nursing practice experience. • Minimum of five (5) years of experience in academic education. • Experience in academic and/or healthcare administration preferred. • Demonstrated enthusiasm for serving a diverse student and client population. • Excellent written and verbal communication skills. • Strong interpersonal and people-management skills. • Ability to draft reports and correspondence and speak effectively to diverse constituencies. • Ability to manage confidential and sensitive matters with judgment, tact, and diplomacy. • Strong organizational skills with the ability to multi-task, meet deadlines, and prioritize responsibilities. • Ability to facilitate teamwork in an environment addressing a broad range of academic and operational issues. • Proficiency in advanced functions of Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Excel, and Outlook. The position of Dean, School of Nursing and Health Sciences involves a combination of sedentary office work and active engagement across campus and external locations. The role requires the ability to sit, stand, walk, speak, hear, and use hands and fingers for standard office functions such as computer use and document handling. Occasional lifting of materials up to approximately 25 pounds may be required. The position involves frequent interaction with faculty, staff, students, and external partners, and may require extended periods of concentration, decision-making, and communication. Travel to meetings, conferences, and clinical or community partner sites occurs on an occasional basis. The work environment is primarily an office and academic setting with standard safety conditions. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Saint Xavier University is committed to providing employees with a comprehensive benefits package that meets the needs of both the individual and his/her family. Many of the benefits are flexible and offer choices to meet various benefit needs. SXU employment benefits can be found here . Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3450 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sxuedu/jobs/5503376/lecturer-exercise-science": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Exercise Science",
      "description": "Lecturer-Exercise Science Salary $59,000.00 Annually Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 01655 Department SONHS - Exercise Science and Sports and Fitness Administration Opening Date 10/02/2026 Description Benefits Summary Founded in 1847 by the Sisters of Mercy, Saint Xavier University is the oldest Catholic Institution in Chicago. As a Catholic University and a Sisters of Mercy institution, SXU drives the mission of community, teaching, learning and research. Saint Xavier University seeks applicants for a full-time 9-month Non-Tenure Assistant Professorial Lecturer position within Exercise Science to begin in August 2026. The Exercise Science Division is within the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. The Exercise Science Division includes majors in exercise science (undergraduate and graduate), Sports Management, Physical Education, and a Strength and Conditioning Minor. The objective of the Exercise Science Division at Saint Xavier University is to equip students with the knowledge, skills, and practical application necessary for today’s entry-level exercise science careers. The Exercise Science program is part of the National Strength and Conditioning Associations Educational Recognized Program (ERP) in which students will establish evidence-based practices, scientific knowledge, and practical work experience to bridge the gap between science and application. Program faculty are expected to work collaboratively with each other, faculty outside of the program, and community partners. . Essential Duties & Responsibilities o Teach in undergrad and graduate Exercise Science program. o Serve as a mentor to students in the Exercise Science Division o Participate in research and scholarship. o Provide service to the University, community, and profession. o Perform other duties as designated by the Dean and/or Director of Exercise Science. o Support Saint Xavier University’s core values of Respect, Excellence, Compassion, Service, Hospitality, Integrity, Diversity, and Learning for Life. Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities who are otherwise qualified to perform the essential functions. 1. Master’s degree within the health field (instructor-level), Ph.D., preferred (Assistant Professor). 2. Focus on (but not limited to) the areas of biomechanics, strength and conditioning, exercise physiology, research methods, and nutrition. 3. Teaching experience at the Higher Education level of 3 years or professional experience within the health and wellness field of 3 years. 4. Certification of ACSM or NSCA is preferred 5. Knowledge of Word, PowerPoint, Adobe, Excel, and Outlook 6. Excellent written and verbal communication skills Physical Demands: Nearly continuously: sitting, hearing, listening, talking, and interacting with students, faculty, staff, and other constituents across the University. Items to include in the application: 1. A letter of interest describing qualifications and accomplishments 2. A curriculum vitae 3. Short (1-page) teaching philosophy statement 4. Documents showing evidence of teaching effectiveness 5. Short description of Scholarship plans and research capabilities 6. Samples of scholarly or creative work (e.g. documents, video, etc.) 7. Unofficial Graduate transcripts 8. A list of three professional references (included in the application): Name, Organization, Email address and Telephone Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Saint Xavier University is committed to providing employees with a comprehensive benefits package that meets the needs of both the individual and his/her family. Many of the benefits are flexible and offer choices to meet various benefit needs. SXU employment benefits can be found here . Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3450 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sxuedu/jobs/5451843/vocational-specialist": {
      "title": "Vocational Specialist",
      "description": "Vocational Specialist Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 01614 Department SONHS - Communication Sciences & Disorders Opening Date 08/18/2026 Per Credit Hour $1,080.00 Summary The Vocational Specialist manages the Community of Adult Cougars Helping (C.O.A.C.H.) specialty clinic operations and provides administrative support to the faculty and graduate students within the Communication Sciences & Disorders Program. This individual supports Ludden Speech & Language Clients with disabilities and communication barriers with the goal of building skills, workplace relationship, and independence leading to employment. Manages multiple responsibilities while interacting with clients, students and faculty in a busy academic and clinic environment. This is a grant funded position. Monday 8:30 – 12:30, fall semester 2026 Essential Duties & Responsibilities 1. Create connections and secure sites for the placement of adult clients with disabilities to provide a clinical site for SXU SLP students to gain clinical experience while adult clients develop communication skills required for employment. 2. Share success stories and act as an advisor for other interested employers. 3. Create an intake process for the functional assessment of clients who apply to the program for admission. 4. Develop and maintain vocational training curriculum. 5. Coach, encourage and support individuals on and off the job sites to help them build professionalism, interpersonal skills and gain independence. 6. Provide one-on-one, hands-on instruction at the job site to help the individual learn specific tasks and meet employer expectations. 7. Help clients navigate social dynamics, advocate for necessary accommodations, and communicate effectively with supervisors. 8. Investigate the feasibility of support for parent guidance on finding employment for adult children. 9. Encourage problem solving to work through issues that arise. 10. Provide positive feedback and areas for improvement related to the individual’s performance and employer expectations. 11. Create and update records and reports on progress. 12. Coordinate and monitor transportation as this can be a barrier to site placement. 13. Coordinate team building events and activities as appropriate. 14. Complete all other duties or assigned as needed. Qualifications College degree in social work required. Three or more years of related experience working with adults with disabilities in a school or clinic setting. Knowledge of Illinois programs of adults with disabilities. Exceptional communication skills (oral and written), organizational, interpersonal and time management skills. Attention to detail and ability to multi-task, meet deadlines, work independently, and prioritize. Ability to work with a diverse population in a professional, courteous, and tactful manner. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3450 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/sxuedu/jobs/5532393/social-work-faculty-program-director": {
      "title": "Social Work Faculty Program Director",
      "description": "Social Work Faculty Program Director Salary $85,000.00 - $90,000.00 Annually Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number 01676 Department Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/28/2026 Description Benefits Summary The College of Liberal Arts and Education at Saint Xavier University invites applications for a full-time open rank faculty program director of the developing Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) program. We specifically seek a faculty member with significant experience in or aptitude for Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) program development, curriculum design, field education, and assessment to support the intentional development of a new social work program to serve as the BSW Program Director. The position can either be a tenure-track position, in which a doctorate is required in addition to an MSW, or a professional practice position, which is a long-term professional appointment, in which a doctorate is not necessarily required in addition to an MSW. The director position is currently set at an 11-month position which includes teaching 9 credits each semester (fall and spring) with a 3-credit course release in fall and spring for director duties. The position is planned to start January 1, 2027, for the Spring 2027 semester. Saint Xavier University was founded by the Sisters of Mercy in 1846 and is guided by fundamental values of the Sisters to serve the underserved. Saint Xavier University is a Hispanic Serving Institution and is recognized as a top performer on social mobility and one of the most diverse student populations among regional universities in the Midwest by U.S. News & World Report. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Lead the development and accreditation of a new BSW curriculum, including syllabi, curriculum, curricular alignment to CSWE competencies, and accreditation materials Teach undergraduate courses in Sociology and Social Work Perform service to the department, college, and university For a tenure-track appointment, conduct scholarship to meet tenure requirements For a professional practice appointment, engage in professional outreach related to Social Work Qualifications MSW from a CSWE-accredited program; Doctorate preferred and required for a tenure-track appointment At least two years of post-master’s social work degree practice experience in social work Demonstrated experience in or potential for BSW program development or leadership, including curriculum design and field education. Substantive experience with assessment, accreditation preparation, and competency-based evaluation. Preferred Qualifications Prior leadership in launching or significantly developing a social work program. Experience supporting pathways from BSW to MSW program development. Application Materials Please provide a cover letter which addresses experience or ability to develop a BSW program, including accreditation; CV; teaching philosophy; and contact information for three letters of recommendation. Letters of recommendation will be solicited at a later date for finalists. Please name files as “Lastname_CV,” etc. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Angela Pirlott, Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Education and search committee chair, at Pirlott@sxu.edu. Deadline Review of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision, and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bonafide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Saint Xavier University is committed to providing employees with a comprehensive benefits package that meets the needs of both the individual and his/her family. Many of the benefits are flexible and offer choices to meet various benefit needs. SXU employment benefits can be found here . Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3450 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply"
    }
